    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `membershipTier` derived field on the owner response.\n\n**What \"derived read-only field\" looks like in this codebase:** fields like `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipNumber` are defined in the OpenAPI schema (which generates `OwnerDto`) and computed in `OwnerMapper` via MapStruct expressions \u2014 the entity itself isn't touched. I followed that same pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipTier` property to the `Owner` schema with an `enum: [SILVER, BRONZE]`, so the generator produces `OwnerDto.MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `membershipTier` backed by a `toMembershipTier(owner)` helper:\n   - `SILVER` when `namesakeCount == 0` **and** email is present,\n   - `BRONZE` otherwise (including null/absent namesakeCount, e.g. unmigrated seed data \u2014 treated as not-unique, which is the safe default).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests pass:\n- `coreSilverWhenUniqueWithEmail` \u2014 unique owner (namesakeCount 0) + email \u2192 `SILVER`\n- `functionalityBronzeWhenNoEmail` \u2014 no email \u2192 `BRONZE`\n\nNo changes were needed to the OfficeFloor pipeline itself: `AssignNamesakeCount` already sets the count during `POST`, and the tier is computed at mapping time on every read.",
